{"id":"h3-09-o1","title":"Object storage and blobs","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: S3-style design, chunking, multipart upload, presigned URLs, tiers and cost. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"what-object-storage-is","title":"What object storage is","html":"<p><strong>Object storage keeps whole files (\"objects\") in a flat namespace of buckets and keys, accessed over HTTP.</strong> There are no real folders and no in-place edits: you PUT a whole object, GET it back (optionally a byte range), DELETE it, LIST by prefix. Each object has data, a key (<code>photos/2026/11/cat.jpg</code>), and metadata.</p>\n<p>Compare with the other two storage kinds:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Block (EBS)</th>\n<th>File (NFS, EFS)</th>\n<th>Object (S3, GCS, Azure Blob)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Access</td>\n<td>Raw disk to one VM</td>\n<td>Mounted folders, POSIX</td>\n<td>HTTP API with keys</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Edit in place</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No, replace whole object</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Scale</td>\n<td>TB per volume</td>\n<td>PB, but costly</td>\n<td>Effectively unlimited</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cost per GB-month</td>\n<td>highest</td>\n<td>middle</td>\n<td>lowest (S3 Standard about $0.023)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 490 130\" width=\"490\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Typical use: app stores a pointer, not the bytes\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M268.4 34 L324.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M268.4 34 L324.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Object store</text><rect x=\"324.4\" y=\"43\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"401.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Postgres: file key</text></svg><figcaption>Typical use: app stores a pointer, not the bytes</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 50M users upload an average 2 MB photo: 100 TB. In Postgres BLOBs that would wreck backups and cache. In S3 Standard: 100,000 GB x $0.023 = about $2,300/month. The database stores only <code>photo_key</code> (about 60 bytes), so 50M rows is 3 GB.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Amazon S3 (launched 2006, many trillions of objects), Google Cloud Storage, Azure Blob, MinIO/Ceph for self-hosting. Dropbox stored files in S3 and later built its own storage system (Magic Pocket) once scale made it cheaper. Netflix keeps masters and encodes in S3.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A coat check: hand over the whole coat, get a ticket (key), return the ticket for the whole coat. You can not sew one button on while it hangs in the cloakroom.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Storing large binary files in the relational database.</li>\n<li>Treating S3 prefixes as real directories (renaming a \"folder\" is copy plus delete of every object).</li>\n<li>Assuming you can append or edit a few bytes.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"how-an-s3-like-system-is-built-inside","title":"How an S3-like system is built inside","html":"<p><strong>Three layers: a front-end API tier, a metadata service mapping keys to storage locations, and a data tier of many storage nodes holding the bytes.</strong></p>\n<p>Flow of a PUT:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Load balancer and API server authenticate (signature) and authorize (IAM/bucket policy).</li>\n<li>Data is split into chunks (for example 64 MB or smaller), each written to several storage nodes.</li>\n<li>Metadata (bucket, key, size, checksum, chunk locations, version) is written to a strongly consistent, sharded metadata store.</li>\n<li>Only after enough copies are durable does the API return 200.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 650.4 254\" width=\"650.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"PUT path\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 127 L158 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 127 L158 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 127 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 127 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M443.2 34 L499.2 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M443.2 34 L499.2 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 127 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 127 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 127 L304 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 127 L304 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 127 L304 220\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 127 L304 220\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"105\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"105\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">API tier</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"373.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Metadata service</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"74\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"373.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Storage node 1</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"136\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"373.6\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Storage node 2</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"198\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"373.6\" y=\"224\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Storage node 3</text><rect x=\"499.2\" y=\"105\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"568.8\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Key to chunk map</text></svg><figcaption>PUT path</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Durability.</strong> S3 advertises 99.999999999% (eleven nines) durability: expected loss of one object per 10 million objects every 10,000 years. It comes from redundancy across at least 3 availability zones, checksums on every read/write, constant background scrubbing and repair when a disk dies.</p>\n<p><strong>Replication vs erasure coding.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>3x replication: 200% overhead, simple, fast reads and repair.</li>\n<li>Erasure coding (Reed-Solomon k+m): split data into k data pieces plus m parity pieces; any k of k+m recover the object. With 10+4: overhead 40%, tolerates 4 lost pieces. Used for large cold data; costs CPU and slower repairs.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Object 100 MB -> 10 data shards (10 MB) + 4 parity shards (10 MB)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Stored: 140 MB (1.4x). Survives any 4 shard losses.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>3x replication would store 300 MB (3x).</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Consistency.</strong> S3 was eventually consistent for overwrite and delete until December 2020; since then it provides strong read-after-write consistency for PUT, DELETE and LIST. GCS has had strong consistency for years.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 1 PB of data: replication needs 3 PB raw; 10+4 erasure coding needs 1.4 PB, saving 1.6 PB of disks, around thousands of drives. That is why hyperscalers use EC for warm and cold tiers.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Choosing replication for hot small objects and EC for big cold ones is reversible (background transition). The metadata store design (sharded, consistent) is the hard part and a one-way door; most object store outages are metadata or index-related, not data-related.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> S3's internals are partly public (re:Invent talks: ShardStore, a Rust key-value storage node; formal verification), Facebook's f4 and Haystack for photos (Haystack packed many photos into big files to avoid a metadata lookup per photo), Ceph RADOS, MinIO erasure sets.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A library that tears each book into sections, stores copies in different buildings, and keeps an index card that says where each piece is.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forgetting the metadata layer is the bottleneck, not the disks.</li>\n<li>Quoting eleven nines as availability; it is durability, availability is about 99.99%.</li>\n<li>Confusing replication with erasure coding overhead.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"chunking-and-multipart-upload","title":"Chunking and multipart upload","html":"<p><strong>Big files are split into parts that upload in parallel and can be retried individually.</strong> A single PUT of a 5 GB file over a flaky mobile connection would restart from zero on any failure.</p>\n<p>S3 multipart upload:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><code>CreateMultipartUpload</code> returns an <code>UploadId</code>.</li>\n<li><code>UploadPart</code> for parts 1..N (each 5 MiB to 5 GiB except the last; up to 10,000 parts; max object 5 TiB). Each part returns an ETag.</li>\n<li><code>CompleteMultipartUpload</code> with the ordered list of part numbers and ETags; S3 stitches them.</li>\n<li><code>AbortMultipartUpload</code> frees orphaned parts. Add a lifecycle rule to auto-abort incomplete uploads after 7 days, else you pay for invisible parts.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 406 192\" width=\"406\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Parallel part upload\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 96 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 96 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 158 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 158 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Part 1</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Part 2</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"136\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Part 3</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">S3</text></svg><figcaption>Parallel part upload</figcaption></figure>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># AWS CLI does multipart automatically over the threshold</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">aws</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> configure</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> set</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> default.s3.multipart_threshold</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> 64MB</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">aws</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> configure</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> set</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> default.s3.multipart_chunksize</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> 16MB</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">aws</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> configure</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> set</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> default.s3.max_concurrent_requests</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 20</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">aws</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> s3</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> cp</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> movie.mkv</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> s3://my-bucket/raw/movie.mkv</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 4 GB file, 16 MB parts = 256 parts. At 5 parts in parallel and 20 MB/s each (100 MB/s total) it takes about 41 s instead of about 200 s at one stream. If part 137 fails at 99%, retry only that 16 MB.</p>\n<p><strong>Resumable uploads and chunk design for your own service.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Choose chunk size by network: 5 to 8 MB for mobile (small retry cost), 16 to 64 MB for datacenter.</li>\n<li>Content hashing: SHA-256 per chunk lets the server say \"I already have this chunk\" (deduplication) and verify integrity. Dropbox-style sync uses 4 MB blocks with hashes so a small edit uploads one block, not the whole file.</li>\n<li>Resumable protocols: tus.io, Google's resumable upload (session URI, ask server for received offset).</li>\n<li>Track state: <code>upload_id</code>, parts received, expiry, owner in a database or Redis.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// Android: upload part with retry; each part independent</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">suspend</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> fun</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> uploadPart</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(url: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">String</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, bytes: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ByteArray</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, attempt: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">): </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">String</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    val</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> resp </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> http.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">put</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(url, bytes)          </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// presigned URL for this part</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    if</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (resp.isSuccessful) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> resp.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">header</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"ETag\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">!!</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    if</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (attempt </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">>=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 4</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">error</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"part failed\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">    delay</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">500L</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> shl attempt)                  </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// exponential backoff</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> uploadPart</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(url, bytes, attempt </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">+</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> S3/GCS multipart, YouTube resumable uploads, Dropbox 4 MB block sync with content hashes, WhatsApp media upload with resume, Netflix chunk-based parallel ingest of masters.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Chunk size is reversible per upload, but changing a content-defined chunking scheme later breaks deduplication of existing data. Multipart adds state to manage (orphan parts); the alternative of single PUT is fine under about 100 MB.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Moving house with ten helpers carrying different boxes at once, and re-carrying only the one box that was dropped.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Using single PUT for multi-GB files.</li>\n<li>Forgetting to abort incomplete multipart uploads (hidden cost).</li>\n<li>Not verifying checksums at the end.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"presigned-urls-and-direct-uploads","title":"Presigned URLs and direct uploads","html":"<p><strong>A presigned URL is a temporary link, signed with your secret key, that lets someone do one specific operation on one object without having credentials.</strong></p>\n<p>Why: without it, a 2 GB upload flows client to your app server to S3, tying up your bandwidth, threads and cost. With it, the client uploads directly to S3; your server only issues the URL.</p>\n<p>Flow:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Client asks API: \"I want to upload <code>cat.jpg</code>, 3 MB, image/jpeg\".</li>\n<li>API checks the user, allowed type and size, picks a key <code>u/{userId}/{uuid}.jpg</code>, creates a presigned PUT URL valid for 15 minutes, and stores a pending record.</li>\n<li>Client PUTs bytes straight to S3.</li>\n<li>S3 event (ObjectCreated) triggers a Lambda/queue; backend marks the record uploaded, creates thumbnails, scans for malware.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 664.8 130\" width=\"664.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Direct upload with presigned URL\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M254 34 L310 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M254 34 L310 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M254 96 L310 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M254 96 L310 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M506.8 96 L562.8 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M506.8 96 L562.8 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">API server</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">S3 bucket</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"12\" width=\"196.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"408.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Postgres: pending upload</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"74\" width=\"196.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"408.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Event queue</text><rect x=\"562.8\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"607.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Processor</text></svg><figcaption>Direct upload with presigned URL</figcaption></figure>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// AWS SDK v2: presigned PUT, 15 minutes</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">PutObjectRequest put </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> PutObjectRequest.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">builder</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    .</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">bucket</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"media-prod\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">).</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">key</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"u/42/9f1c.jpg\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    .</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">contentType</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"image/jpeg\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">).</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">build</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">PresignedPutObjectRequest p </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> presigner.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">presignPutObject</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(r </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">-></span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> r</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    .</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">signatureDuration</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(Duration.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ofMinutes</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">15</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    .</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">putObjectRequest</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(put));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">String url </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> p.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">url</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">().</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">toString</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">();</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Security controls:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Short expiry (minutes for uploads; reads maybe hours).</li>\n<li>Fix the key server-side; never let the client choose the path.</li>\n<li>Presigned POST policies can enforce a content-length range and content type.</li>\n<li>Remember the URL is a bearer token: anyone who has it can use it until expiry. Use HTTPS only.</li>\n<li>Validate after upload (type sniffing, size, virus scan); the client can lie about content type.</li>\n<li>For downloads of private files, serve through a CDN with signed URLs/cookies (CloudFront signed URLs).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 10,000 uploads/hour at 3 MB = 30 GB/h through the app server would need roughly 67 Mbit/s sustained plus connection handling; presigned direct upload cuts app traffic to 10,000 tiny JSON calls.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Instagram and Slack-style apps use direct-to-S3 uploads; Android apps upload via presigned URLs from WorkManager with retry; CloudFront signed URLs protect Netflix-like paid content; GCS \"signed URLs\" are the same idea.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Reversible and recommended default. Alternative is proxying through the app, only sensible for tiny files or when you must inspect bytes inline.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A valet ticket valid for one car, for one hour, which any person holding it can use.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Long-lived presigned URLs (days) that leak.</li>\n<li>Trusting the client's content type or size.</li>\n<li>Not handling the case where a client gets a URL but never uploads (pending records need a cleanup job).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"storage-classes-lifecycle-cdn-and-cost","title":"Storage classes, lifecycle, CDN and cost","html":"<p><strong>Not all data is accessed equally, so object stores offer tiers with different price and retrieval cost.</strong></p>\n<p>S3 tiers (prices approximate, check current): Standard (about $0.023/GB-month), Standard-IA/infrequent (about $0.0125, retrieval fee, 30-day minimum), Glacier Instant/Flexible/Deep Archive (down to about $0.001/GB-month, retrieval takes minutes to 12+ hours), Intelligent-Tiering (auto-moves by access).</p>\n<p><strong>Lifecycle rule example.</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"Rules\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">    \"ID\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"tier-and-expire\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">    \"Status\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Enabled\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">    \"Filter\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: {</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"Prefix\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"logs/\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">},</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">    \"Transitions\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">      {</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"Days\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">30</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"StorageClass\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"STANDARD_IA\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">},</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">      {</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"Days\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">90</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"StorageClass\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"GLACIER\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    ],</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">    \"Expiration\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: {</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"Days\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">365</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">},</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">    \"AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: {</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"DaysAfterInitiation\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">7</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  }]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Serving files.</strong> Put a CDN (CloudFront, Cloudflare, Fastly) in front: edge cache hit ratio of 95% means 20x fewer origin requests and much cheaper egress. Set <code>Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable</code> and use content-hashed keys (<code>app.3f9a.js</code>) so you never need to invalidate.</p>\n<p><strong>Request limits and key design.</strong> S3 supports at least 3,500 PUT/POST/DELETE and 5,500 GET/HEAD requests per second per prefix, and scales by prefix. Old advice to randomize key prefixes is no longer needed, but spread heavy traffic across prefixes anyway. LIST is slow and costly; keep an index in a database for queries like \"all photos of user 42\".</p>\n<p><strong>Other features:</strong> versioning (undo overwrite/delete), object lock (WORM compliance), cross-region replication (disaster recovery), server-side encryption (SSE-S3 or KMS), event notifications.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 621.6 68\" width=\"621.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cost-aware lifecycle\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M136.8 34 L192.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M136.8 34 L192.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M282.8 34 L338.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M282.8 34 L338.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M463.6 34 L519.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M463.6 34 L519.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"74.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Hot (Standard)</text><rect x=\"192.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"237.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Warm (IA)</text><rect x=\"338.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"401.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Cold (Glacier)</text><rect x=\"519.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"564.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Deleted</text></svg><figcaption>Cost-aware lifecycle</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 500 TB of logs. All Standard: 500,000 x 0.023 = $11,500/month. After 90 days 90% sits in Glacier at ~$0.004: 450,000 x 0.004 + 50,000 x 0.023 = 1,800 + 1,150 = $2,950/month, a 74% saving.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Netflix and Spotify tier old data; CDN-fronted images at Instagram; Cloudflare R2 markets zero egress fees as differentiator.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Lifecycle rules are reversible but retrieval from Glacier is slow/expensive, so a wrongly archived \"hot\" dataset hurts. Egress cost (about $0.09/GB out to the internet on S3) is the hidden big bill; a CDN or private connectivity reduces it.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Keeping this week's clothes in the wardrobe, last season's in the loft, and old school books in a storage unit across town.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignoring egress and request costs.</li>\n<li>Using LIST as a database.</li>\n<li>Forgetting versioned buckets keep deleted data (and bills).</li>\n<li>Archiving data that is read frequently.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Object storage = keys to whole immutable objects over HTTP; cheap, huge, durable; not a filesystem, no in-place edit.</li>\n<li>Inside: API tier, strongly consistent sharded metadata, chunked data with replication or erasure coding across AZs.</li>\n<li>Multipart upload: parallel, resumable parts (5 MiB to 5 GiB, up to 10,000), abort leftovers, checksum chunks.</li>\n<li>Presigned URLs send bytes straight to storage; keep them short-lived, fix keys server-side, validate afterwards.</li>\n<li>Control cost with lifecycle tiers, CDN caching and attention to egress; keep a DB index instead of LIST.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}